REGRESSION CANDIDATE 1 — CONFIRMED (pre-existing, out of NEARS-645 scope)
ItemCard lets you add an OUT-OF-STOCK item to the cart; the "+" stays an ACTIVE mint
circle (ItemWidget shows a disabled grey 0.4-opacity circle for stock<=0).

Surface: Burger Palace store profile -> "Recommended For You" rail (inStore ItemCard),
zone 1 (Demo Zone — Dhaka), Food module. Item: Double Bacon Burger (id 17, stock=0).
Code: item_card.dart:166-199 wraps CartCountView with no out-of-stock disabled branch
(cf. item_widget.dart:412-461 which gates on `outOfStock`).

Live repro:
1. Card shows "Out of Stock" overlay AND an active mint "+" (screenshot 07).
2. Tapped "+" on the out-of-stock card -> cross-store "Start a new basket?" dialog (the
   tap was honored; stock was NOT a gate). Tapped Yes.
3. App logcat (flutter):
   ====> API Response: [200] /api/v1/customer/cart/remove
   ====> API Response: [200] /api/v1/customer/cart/add
   analytics: add_to_cart {item_id: 17, price: 12.99, quantity: 1, currency: AED, value: 12.99}
   ====> API Response: [200] /api/v1/customer/cart/list
   (no [FAIL]/[ERR] — the add succeeded silently)
4. DB confirm (read-only SELECT) — cart for customer@nears.com now contains:
   item_id 17  Double Bacon Burger  stock=0  quantity=1
   => an out-of-stock item is in the cart.

Impact: a user can add a sold-out item to the basket from any ItemCard rail. ItemWidget
prevents this. Fix would mirror ItemWidget's outOfStock-disabled branch into ItemCard.
